    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-apply-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1520,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### check_in\n_What are you working on, and what do you need from the library?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- nothing: advance\n\n**Gate uses:** `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-apply-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1520,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### find\n_Find, qualify, open, extract: which sources did you use, and for what?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- log the sources you used (log_use), or update_plan(fields={'nothing_found': ...})\n\n**Gate uses:** `log_use`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `log_use`, `read_source_file`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-apply-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1520,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### check_out\n_What did the library fail to answer?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- record_application, or update_plan(fields={'no_application': reason})\n\n**Gate uses:** `record_application`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `close_session`, `get_note`, `record_application`, `staging_list`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-apply",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 980,
      "label": "apply session"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-start_pursuit-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2020,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### frame\n_Which project is this for, what stage is it at, and what is fixed?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- no Project note for 'P': create_project\n\n**Gate uses:** `create_project`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `create_project`, `get_note`, `search`, `session_status`, `topics_list`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-start_pursuit-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2020,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### inventory\n_Kind-specific questions: what does this pursuit actually involve - modules and assessments, a role and its first-90-days, deliverables and stakeholders, or a research question and what's already known?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- record the kind-specific inventory: update_plan(fields={'inventory': ...})\n- before committing: record what you are assuming and how each was settled - record_assumptions([{assumption, settled_by, how}]), where settled_by is a tool you called here, an answered question's id, or 'unverifiable' (an empty list if you assume nothing)\n\n**Gate uses:** `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `read_source_file`, `record_assumptions`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-start_pursuit-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2020,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### plan\n_What are the milestones, and which of them have dates?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- add at least one dated milestone (task_add), or update_plan(fields={'no_dates': reason})\n\n**Gate uses:** `task_add`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `search`, `task_add`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-start_pursuit-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2020,
      "y": 980,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### seed\n_What reading, handbooks or onboarding material belongs in the library for this pursuit, and which of it matters enough to pin to the desk?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- record what was seeded: update_plan(fields={'ingested': ...}) (a list, or 'none')\n\n**Gate uses:** `ingest`, `queue_source`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `ingest`, `queue_source`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-start_pursuit-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2020,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### check_out\n_What did the library fail to answer?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- nothing: advance\n\n**Gate uses:** \n\n**Tools:** `close_brief`, `close_session`, `get_note`, `record_application`, `staging_list`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-start_pursuit",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 2000,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 1580,
      "label": "start_pursuit session"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### goal\n_What do they want to be able to do, and by when?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- what do they want to be able to do, and by when: update_plan(fields={'goal': ..., 'deadline': ...})\n\n**Gate uses:** `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### baseline\n_Before teaching anything: 2-3 questions on what they already know._\n\n**To leave:**\n- 2-3 diagnostic questions before teaching: ask_user, then update_plan(fields={'baseline': ...})\n\n**Gate uses:** `ask_user`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### focus\n_What does the library hold on this, and which concepts should this session focus on?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- read what the library holds, then choose the focus concepts: update_plan(fields={'focus': [...]})\n\n**Gate uses:** `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `read_source_file`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 980,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### practice\n_Ask one question anchored in a source passage; the person answers; feedback cites the passage; record what they understand._\n\n**To leave:**\n- nothing: advance\n\n**Gate uses:** `understanding_record`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `read_source_file`, `search`, `understanding_record`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### consolidate\n_Let the person explain it in their own words first; critique it against the sources, grounded like the scribe._\n\n**To leave:**\n- let them explain it in their own words, critique it against the sources, then understanding_record and update_plan(fields={'consolidated': ...})\n\n**Gate uses:** `understanding_record`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `read_source_file`, `search`, `understanding_record`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 1580,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### next\n_When should this be reviewed again, and is there a next session to propose?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- review dates as tasks - task_add(note='<project note>', text='Review: <concept>', due=..., heading='Understanding') - or enable the Spaced Repetition plugin, then update_plan(fields={'scheduled': ...})\n\n**Gate uses:** `task_add`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `close_session`, `get_note`, `search`, `task_add`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-learn",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 2500,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 1880,
      "label": "learn session"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-add_capability-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3020,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### candidate\n_Which server? One from capability_candidates (the curated list), or a repository URL the person gives - never one found by browsing on your own._\n\n**To leave:**\n- name the candidate: update_plan(fields={'candidate': ...}) - a curated server (capability_candidates) or a repository URL the person gave\n\n**Gate uses:** `capability_candidates`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `capability_candidates`, `get_note`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-add_capability-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3020,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### assess\n_ingest its repository, read it as a source, and record the assessment: licence, maintenance, what it claims, caveats, what it can reach - its card is its own claim, and the narrowest tool that does the job is the one to want._\n\n**To leave:**\n- ingest the candidate's repository, so it is read as a source\n- before committing: record what you are assuming and how each was settled - record_assumptions([{assumption, settled_by, how}]), where settled_by is a tool you called here, an answered question's id, or 'unverifiable' (an empty list if you assume nothing)\n\n**Gate uses:** `ingest`, `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `get_note`, `ingest`, `read_source_file`, `record_assumptions`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-add_capability-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3020,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### propose\n_Propose one exact, pinned definition: which launcher, which version, which secrets (as ${ENV} names only), and why this library needs it._\n\n**To leave:**\n- propose its exact definition: capability_propose(...)\n\n**Gate uses:** `capability_propose`\n\n**Tools:** `capability_propose`, `get_note`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-add_capability-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3020,
      "y": 980,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### install\n_The person decides: capability_install asks them, and installs only on yes._\n\n**To leave:**\n- capability_install(name) - it asks the person; a decline is a finished outcome too\n\n**Gate uses:** `capability_install`\n\n**Tools:** `capability_install`, `get_note`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-add_capability-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3020,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### check_out\n_What did the library fail to answer?_\n\n**To leave:**\n- nothing: advance\n\n**Gate uses:** `close_brief`\n\n**Tools:** `close_brief`, `close_session`, `get_note`, `record_application`, `staging_list`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-add_capability",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 3000,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 1580,
      "label": "add_capability session"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-audited-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### manage\n_Which open requirement comes next, and what one bounded step serves it? Record it with update_plan(fields={'proposal': {'requirements': [...], 'step': ...}}); ask the person instead if the requirement is unclear._\n\n**To leave:**\n- no requirements yet: the person sets them with set_requirement\n\n**Gate uses:** `update_plan`\n\n**Tools:** `audit_projection`, `get_note`, `read_evidence`, `search`, `update_plan`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-audited-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### preflight\n_The Core admits the proposal as a contract against the current state, or refuses it with the reason._\n\n**To leave:**\n- no contract has been admitted: preflight admits one\n\n**Gate uses:** `admit_contract`\n\n**Tools:** `admit_contract`, `audit_projection`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-audited-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### execute\n_Do only what the admitted contract allows, through its tools._\n\n**To leave:**\n- no contract has been admitted: preflight admits one\n\n**Gate uses:** `stage_artifact`\n\n**Tools:** `dispatch_plan`, `get_note`, `read_evidence`, `read_source_file`, `request_raw_source_access`, `search`, `source_verification_plan`, `stage_artifact`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-audited-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 980,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### audit\n_Tier A checks every predicate of the contract's requirements on the actual artifacts; a missing or failed check is recorded, not skipped._\n\n**To leave:**\n- no contract has been admitted: preflight admits one\n\n**Gate uses:** `audit_targets`, `verify_grain`\n\n**Tools:** `audit_projection`, `audit_targets`, `verify_grain`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-audited-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "### reduce\n_The Core turns the round's results into requirement statuses. Then start the next round, or close the session if every requirement is accounted for._\n\n**To leave:**\n- no contract has been admitted: preflight admits one\n\n**Gate uses:** `close_session`, `reduce_round`\n\n**Tools:** `audit_projection`, `close_session`, `reduce_round`"
    },
    {
      "id": "librarian-map-audited",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 3500,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 1580,
      "label": "audited session"
    }
  ],
